invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: the Initial key's constructor never records the session's description
  of the CPU in a schedule, so the schedule reads what its storage held,
  and gcm.c picks its whole-block path from that. bin/aes_runtime_test
  fills the key with 0xff before the call and requires both schedules'
  cpu byte to hold the value the call was given.

--- old
    s->cpu = (uint8_t)cpu;
--- new
